<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:14.4pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Xunlei Limited</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Notes&#160;to the consolidated financial statements</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">(Amounts in US dollars unless otherwise stated)</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="Tc_n7m-cLakgkWkNQRTxBcRnQ_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_VyGAaToI3UeZNhna65-TPA_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_DBxWnetQMUy_bhnOrxtZ2w_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_ioNx5BUflUan8-clEVrRZg_2_4"></a><a id="Tc_zEgp_i0GZ0-dqqVIeZ2_Eg_2_6"></a><a id="Tc_MCqwDZlOJ0254wBfgolLiA_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_2_Qj4wCMS0KT03isiZavGw_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_Fh8i_qBBpk-j9gliJTKshg_5_0"></a><ix:continuation id="Tb_R32oBe-ImUmocETDTEwu3g_cont1" continuedAt="Tb_R32oBe-ImUmocETDTEwu3g_cont2"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">22.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Taxation (Continued)</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">(v)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;PRC Enterprise Income Tax (&#8220;EIT&#8221;)</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The EIT is calculated based on the taxable income determined under the PRC laws and accounting standards.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Under the EIT Law, foreign invested enterprises and domestic enterprises are subject to a unified EIT rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_s84E49noE0C5LJg3V9vbAA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_HhXRrFg-FkiRysXg5qwFIA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_-WXaVks7ZEWwFY3NBhbWsw">25</ix:nonFraction>%. In accordance with the implementation rules&#160;of the EIT Law, a qualified &#8220;High and New Technology Enterprise&#8221; (&#8220;HNTE&#8221;) is eligible for a preferential tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_s84E49noE0C5LJg3V9vbAA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_xnet_IncomeTaxPreferredGroupsAxis_xnet_HighAndNewTechnologyEnterprisesMember_TJy5armDqEmk65fV1sFFfg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xnet:PreferentialStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_PL6VAnucM0-bWsfW_83P5g">15</ix:nonFraction>%.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The qualification as an HNTE is subject to annual evaluation and a three-year review by the relevant authorities in China. Shenzhen Xunlei, Shenzhen Onething, Xunlei Computer, Shenzhen Xunlei Wangwenhua Co., Ltd. and Hupu Information were qualified as an HNTE, and enjoyed the preferential tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_s84E49noE0C5LJg3V9vbAA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis_xnet_ShenzhenXunleiShenzhenOnethingXunleiComputerShenzhenXunleiWangwenhuaCoLtdAndHupuShanghaiInformationTechnologyCoLtdMember_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_xnet_IncomeTaxPreferredGroupsAxis_xnet_HighAndNewTechnologyEnterprisesMember_IGrZHHAB5k2pOswEhZWxbA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xnet:PreferentialStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_nblGqigt9EWXmpSLK8uQMQ">15</ix:nonFraction>% for the year ended December 31, 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The majority of the remaining subsidiaries of the Group or VIEs&#8217; subsidiaries in the PRC were qualified for small scale entities and have been granted certain tax concessions by tax authorities in the PRC for the year ended December 31, 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">According to a policy issued by the PRC State Tax Bureau, enterprises engaged in research and development activities are entitled to claim a super deduction of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_s84E49noE0C5LJg3V9vbAA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_xnet_IncomeTaxPreferredGroupsAxis_xnet_ResearchAndDevelopmentEnterpriseActivitiesMember_FHnrCoz-vUuP3FCsL2LRiQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xnet:TaxDeductibleResearchAndDevelopmentExpensePercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_C38RiqvthkSNs_fU3EsNmg">175</ix:nonFraction>% of eligible research and development expenses incurred in a year as tax deductible expenses when calculating taxable income (&#8220;Super Deduction&#8221;), effective from January 1, 2018. Furthermore, beginning October 1, 2022, the super deduction rate was increased to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_s84E49noE0C5LJg3V9vbAA" contextRef="Duration_10_1_2022_To_12_31_2022_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_xnet_IncomeTaxPreferredGroupsAxis_xnet_ResearchAndDevelopmentEnterpriseActivitiesMember_3WuLtkp4jUS-XYKUFDJwPw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xnet:TaxDeductibleResearchAndDevelopmentExpensePercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_U1shbulzH0egZWpknQttvQ">200</ix:nonFraction>%, allowing qualified enterprises to deduct <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_s84E49noE0C5LJg3V9vbAA" contextRef="Duration_10_1_2022_To_12_31_2022_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_xnet_IncomeTaxPreferredGroupsAxis_xnet_ResearchAndDevelopmentEnterpriseActivitiesMember_3WuLtkp4jUS-XYKUFDJwPw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xnet:TaxDeductibleResearchAndDevelopmentExpensePercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_Fmzgn20yEkCqSqRTm5bNBA">200</ix:nonFraction>% of eligible research and development expenses from taxable income for expenses incurred on or after that date.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In addition, according to the EIT Law and its implementation rules, foreign enterprises, which have no establishment or place in the PRC but derive dividends, interest, rents, royalties and other income (including capital gains) from sources in the PRC are subject to PRC withholding tax, or WHT, at <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_s84E49noE0C5LJg3V9vbAA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_HhXRrFg-FkiRysXg5qwFIA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xnet:WithholdingTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_uU1ZTVoVA0WfAyN_9kIhVg">10</ix:nonFraction>% (a further reduced WHT rate may be available according to the applicable double tax treaty arrangement). The <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_s84E49noE0C5LJg3V9vbAA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis_xnet_GiganologyShenzhenAndXunleiComputerMember_aT1CR9IcYUawJKwWvhRdAA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xnet:WithholdingTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_GTSr85FtDE6km-v6-2mSvg">10</ix:nonFraction>% WHT is generally applicable to any dividends to be distributed from Giganology Shenzhen and Xunlei Computer to the Company out of any profits of Giganology Shenzhen and Xunlei Computer derived after January&#160;1, 2008. Up to December 31, 2025, both Giganology Shenzhen and Xunlei Computer did not declare any dividend to the parent company and have determined that they have no present plan to declare and pay any dividends. The Group currently plans to continue to reinvest its subsidiaries&#8217; undistributed earnings, if any, in its operations in China indefinitely. Accordingly, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gRXeGHedr0KrVBeB9p2KmA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_al6_m53bUkK1Txb5nzaONA" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="xnet:WithholdingTaxAccruedOnDividendsReceived" scale="3" id="Narr_L7csfd1fRkiD6h3EM2MZKQ"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gRXeGHedr0KrVBeB9p2KmA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_vbkzi5GMsky01Bj-dNcCJQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="xnet:WithholdingTaxAccruedOnDividendsReceived" scale="3" id="Narr_FIxzdfUnoUWJCfxCQ5vflg"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gRXeGHedr0KrVBeB9p2KmA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_HhXRrFg-FkiRysXg5qwFIA" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="xnet:WithholdingTaxAccruedOnDividendsReceived" scale="3" id="Narr_Ua62VYOdb0i34ba26UY_5w">no</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> withholding income tax was accrued or required to be accrued for the&#160;years ended December 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Moreover, the current EIT Law treats enterprises established outside of China with &#8220;effective management and control&#8221; located in the PRC as PRC resident enterprises for tax purposes. The term &#8220;effective management and control&#8221; is generally defined as exercising overall management and control over the business, personnel, accounting, properties etc. of an enterprise. The Company, if considered a PRC resident enterprise for tax purposes, would be subject to the PRC EIT at the rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_s84E49noE0C5LJg3V9vbAA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_HhXRrFg-FkiRysXg5qwFIA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_BbKV3-7oSkKDUf8s-HHn6w">25</ix:nonFraction>% on its worldwide income for the period after January&#160;1, 2008. As of December 31, 2024 and 2025, the Company has not accrued for PRC tax on such basis. The Company will continue to monitor its tax status.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The current and deferred portions of income tax expenses/(benefits) included in the consolidated statements of operations are as follows:</p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_BKUqmdgPg0KMyqSNWKa1zw" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfComponentsOfIncomeTaxExpenseBenefitTableTextBlock" id="Tb_6W-FD_nXjkClGBET3EPwKQ" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;min-height:0.0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:botto